.TH PDRIVE-APP 1 "October 2026" "PDrive for Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdrive-app \- desktop application of PDrive for Linux (tray icon, status window)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdrive-app
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdrive-app
is the desktop application of PDrive for Linux, an unofficial Proton Drive
client. It runs and supervises
.BR pdrived (1)
(restarting it with an increasing delay if it fails), shows an icon in the
notification area (StatusNotifierItem) and a status window with the account,
used space, recent activity and settings, and lets you sign in and out.
.PP
Only one instance runs: starting the application again shows the status window.
Closing the window does not quit the application; use
.B Quit
in the tray menu, or send
.BR SIGTERM .
The daemon is then stopped cleanly and the drive unmounted.
.PP
On GNOME, the tray icon needs the
.I AppIndicator and KStatusNotifierItem Support
extension. PDrive for Linux is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, Proton AG.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without opening the status window. Used by the autostart entry, which
the settings window creates in
.IR ~/.config/autostart .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PDRIVE_VERBOSE
When set, the daemon logs HTTP requests and SDK debug messages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pdrive/config.toml
Settings, edited by the settings window (see
.BR pdrived (1)).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/pdrive/pdrive.log
Log used when there is no systemd journal (default
.IR ~/.local/state/pdrive/pdrive.log ).
Otherwise, when not started from a terminal, the log of the application and of
the daemon goes to the journal:
.B journalctl \-\-user \-t pdrive
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdrive (1),
.BR pdrived (1)
.PP
https://github.com/bpresles/PDrive\-for\-Linux
